      "message": "Also, with the latest okhttp update, this breaks caching in a very roundabout way (sigh...)\n\nSee OkHttpClient line 129 and OkResponseCacheAdapter from https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/c/59985/3.\n\nSince this object isn\u0027t an instance of c.a.okhttp.HttpResponseCache, it\u0027s wrapped in an OkResponseCacheAdapter, which means that update / trackConditionalHit / trackResponse will never be called on it. That\u0027s not good.\n\nThere\u0027s the obvious workaround of always calling ResponseCache.setDefault( ) with c.a.okhttp.HttpResponseCache objects and using this class as a wrapper, but that will break API users that relied on \u003d\u003d checks.",
